{"seconds": 270.8, "exit": 0, "final": "Excellent! After **Nf7 Kxf7 Bxg5**:\n- Material change: White gained 3 (the bishop)\n- White sacrificed a knight (3) but captured the bishop (3), so material is roughly equal\n- This is a brilliant quiet move creating an unstoppable threat\n\nThe key insight: **Nf7 is a quiet move that appears to sacrifice the knight, but after Black captures with Kxf7 (or other pieces), White recaptures the now-defenseless bishop on g5 with Bxg5, maintaining material balance while achieving superior piece placement.**\n\n**Coaching note (78 words):**\n\n\"Nf7 is a quiet yet devastating move. It forces Black's king to capture the knight (otherwise it's lost), but after Kxf7, White plays Bxg5, recapturing the bishop. The pattern: a quiet move that creates simultaneous threats your opponent cannot address\u2014here, the bishop is left hanging once the king moves. Look for moves that exploit enemy piece coordination. When your opponent's pieces are spread out (like Kg8 and Bg5), they become vulnerable to tactics that remove their key defenders.\"\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nf7\", \"line\": [\"Nf7\", \"Kxf7\", \"Bxg5\", \"Nxg5\", \"Qxg5\"], \"motifs\": [\"quietMove\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "square": "e8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "square": "d5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "square": "e4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1P